From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:20:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 55/55] winewayland: Defer roleless OpenGL client presents.

Black Desert's CEF renderer starts swapping its OpenGL client surface before
the parent window has acquired a live Wayland role. EGL keeps its default
swap interval when disabling it fails, so that early swap can leave EGL's own
frame wait attached to a surface the compositor cannot present. Attaching the
surface later does not recover that wait and the launcher remains blank.

Do not submit ordinary client-surface swaps until the surface is attached to
a toplevel. HWND dma-buf producers remain exempt because their roleless EGL
surface is intentionally used to publish frames through the cross-process
dma-buf path.

This is a narrow adaptation of the OpenGL presentation-suspension behavior
from Wine-Wineland commit aa3013f4bfcb9e2b5dd1ea49a9096d82bc742002 by
Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/opengl.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/opengl.c
index 1865e99..f49d9c1 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/opengl.c
@@ -244,6 +244,9 @@ static BOOL wayland_drawable_swap(struct opengl_drawable *base)
     struct wl_callback *callback;
 
     client_surface_present(base->client);
+    if (!surface->toplevel && !surface->hwnd_dmabuf_producer)
+        return TRUE;
+
     if (!gl->swap_interval_initialized)
     {
         if (funcs->p_eglSwapInterval(egl->display, 0))
